        bpy: 0.80, // Bishnupriya Manipuri (Eastern Indo-Aryan, Bengali / Eastern-Nagari script, ~120k Assam/Tripura+Sylhet) — English Wiktionary "Bishnupriya Manipuri terms with IPA pronunciation" (the ONLY referee — no wikipron/kaikki/epitran bpy; 38 pairs via the MediaWiki API, HUMAN {{IPA|bpy|…}}, ~9 of them single-letter vowel DEFINITIONS = reference-parity) measured 84.2% FOLDED / 95.1% symbol. Reuses the Bengali engine (makeNativeBengali — abugida scan + inherent-vowel deletion + geminate→length) with BENGALI phoneme values (the referee is Bengali-like, NOT Assamese-like): the three sibilants শ/ষ/স→[ʃ] (সাত→ʃat̪, বিশ→biʃ), the affricates চ/ছ/জ→[t͡ʃ t͡ʃʰ d͡ʒ] KEPT (চার→t͡ʃaɾ, হাজার→ɦad͡ʒaɾ), and the retroflex/dental split KEPT (ট→ʈ আট→aʈ vs ত→t̪ তিন→t̪in). The ONE divergence from Bengali proper is heightHarmony:false — the inherent /ɔ/ does NOT raise before a following high/mid vowel (সমুদ্র→ʃɔmud̪ɾo, not ʃomudɾo). Medial + final inherent-vowel deletion behave as Bengali (খরগোশ→kʰɔɾɡoʃ, ফল→pʰɔl). Folds: the referee's retroflex-tinged affricate ⟨ʈʃ⟩→t͡ʃ (চ), the rhotic r~ɾ, geminate CC (দিল্লী), the voiced-breathy notation dʰ~dʱ, the post-vocalic glide→offglide j~i (ছয়→t͡ʃʰɔi), the glottal h~ɦ (পাহাড়), ɪ~i / ʊ~u / ɑ~a. Residual (6, all 1×) = a spelling variant (কঁঠাল read as কাঁঠাল), the referee's [o]-raising of a RETAINED medial inherent (বছর→bɔt͡ʃʰor, মাকড়সা — not Bengali height harmony, which would wrongly raise সমুদ্র), a compound-boundary schwa retention (ভালবাসা), and an intervocalic র→[ɽ] flap (বারো). single-source, THIN (38 pairs, ~29 real) — the % is a real signal on a small HUMAN sample, not a breadth claim. Floor 0.80 (below the 84.2% measured). Deferred: numbers (Bengali-like, unverified), a second referee (none free), the retained-inherent [o] micro-rule.
