        eu: 0.82, // Basque / euskara (eu) — a LANGUAGE ISOLATE (no living relatives), Latin script, highly phonemic orthography. A greedy digraph+letter scan. wikipron eus_latn_broad (HUMAN, 20114): 84.8% FOLDED / 98.0% symbol. THE HALLMARK = the THREE-WAY SIBILANT / affricate system — laminal ⟨z⟩→[s̻] / ⟨tz⟩→[t͡s̻], apical ⟨s⟩→[s̺] / ⟨ts⟩→[t͡s̺], postalveolar ⟨x⟩→[ʃ] / ⟨tx⟩→[t͡ʃ] (zu 'you'→s̻u vs su 'fire'→s̺u; atzo→at͡s̻o vs hots→ot͡s̺). ⟨r⟩ TAP [ɾ] between vowels vs TRILL [r] finally/before-a-consonant/doubled ⟨rr⟩ (udare→udaɾe, hartu→hartu, herri→heri); palatals ⟨tt dd ll ñ⟩→[c ɟ ʎ ɲ]; ⟨j⟩→[x]; ⟨g⟩→[ɡ] always. METRIC NOTE: the referee records each dialectal variant on a SEPARATE ROW (hasi→[as̺i] and [has̺i] are two rows), and this eval scores each row INDEPENDENTLY — it does NOT merge/OR variants per headword (the Galician-style merge was deliberately NOT applied), so 84.8% is a STRICT per-pronunciation number (a best-per-headword reading, ~1.67 prons/word, would be materially higher). THE DIALECT-VARIABLE LETTERS are thus genuine trades, not free: (a) z/s laminal↔apical is WESTERN-NEUTRALISED and the BACKBONE strips the apical/laminal diacritics (U+033A/033B) regardless → both fold to [s] (we EMIT the standard three-way canonically; can't be scored either way); (b) ⟨j⟩→[x] ≈ [j] (a wash, ~equal row counts); (c) ⟨h⟩→[h] wins the h-rows / loses the silent-h rows (measured: [h] 84.84% vs drop 84.19%, faithful to spelling). NO folds. SECONDARY (not floored, 48.0%) = eus_latn_narrow (20079), which marks sub-phonemic ALLOPHONY we don't emit (intervocalic spirantization b→β̞ d→ð̞ g→ɣ̞, dental d̪ n̪, nasalization ẽ õ) — the low % is that depth gap, not a deficiency. Residual = loanword letters (Cancer→soft-c, Abkhazia ⟨kh⟩→x) + the Basque ALPHABET LETTER-NAMES (B→be, C→s̻e, ~27 citations). single-source-FAMILY (broad+narrow both wikipron; epitran eus-Latn datafile absent). Floor 0.82 (below the 84.8% measured). Numbers DONE (the VIGESIMAL base-20 system: 40=berrogei 2