        fo: 0.52, // Faroese / føroyskt (fo) — North Germanic (Insular Scandinavian, sibling of Icelandic), Latin + ⟨á í ó ú ý æ ø ð⟩, ~72k. ONE OF THE DEEPEST orthographies in Europe. THE CORE = vowel LENGTH conditions vowel QUALITY: a stressed vowel is LONG/diphthongal in an OPEN syllable (≤1 following consonant), SHORT/monophthong before a cluster — a→[ɛaː]/[a], á→[ɔɑː]/[ɔ], ó→[ɔuː]/[œ], ú→[ʉuː]/[ʏ], í ý→[ʊiː]/[ʊi], ei→[aiː]/[ai], etc. NO voicing contrast: ⟨b d g⟩→[p t k] (+ pre-aspiration of ⟨p t k⟩, folded). ⟨ð⟩ is largely SILENT (etymological) — intervocalic ⟨ð⟩/⟨g⟩ → the [j]/[v]/∅ glide by the NEIGHBOURING vowel (front i-type {i í y ý ei ey oy æ}→[j]: Eyður→ɛiːjʊɹ; round {o ó u ú ø á}→[v]: dagur→tɛaːvʊɹ; ⟨e a⟩ neutral, defer to the other side: vegur→veːvʊɹ; between ⟨a⟩→∅: agað→ɛaːa). ⟨g k⟩→[t͡ʃ] before a front vowel (argi→aɹt͡ʃɪ; NOT before ⟨ø⟩: gøta→køːta); ⟨tj dj sj⟩→[t͡ʃ d͡ʒ ʃ]; retroflex r-clusters ⟨rn rt rd rs rl⟩→[ɻɳ ʈ ɖ ʂ ɭ]; ⟨ll⟩→[tl]; ⟨v⟩→[u] before a consonant (diphthong); geminate collapse; final -um→[ʊn]. SKERPING ó→[ɛ]/ú→[ɪ] before ⟨gv⟩ (dúgva→tɪkva). ng-palatalization ⟨n⟩→[ɲ]/[ŋ] + a→[ɛ] (gangi→kɛɲt͡ʃɪ). wikipron fao_latn_broad (HUMAN, 3024) — 57.1% FOLDED / 88.6% symbol. THE 88.6% SYMBOL is the HONEST HEADLINE (the Bavarian framing): the folded number is deflated by proper-noun/loan NON-INITIAL stress (Alaska/Benin — engine assumes native initial stress; lowercase-only subset is also 56.7%), the referee's own DIALECTAL MIXING (⟨rn⟩→[tn]~[ɻɳ]: ahorn→ɻɳ but bjørn→tn; ⟨ð⟩→[j]~∅), and fine diphthong-offglide detail. FOLDS: pre-aspiration ʰ, length ː, tie-bar, round-glide w~v, the referee's inconsistent low-vowel backness ɑ~a. single-source FAMILY (wikipron; kaikki fao same Wiktionary source) but LARGE. Floor 0.52 (below the 57.1% measured). Deferred: numbers, a non-initial-stress lexicon (the Norwegian path), the retroflex/[tn] dialect split, compound stress.
