        gd: 0.12, // Scottish Gaelic / Gàidhlig (gd) — Goidelic Celtic (sibling of Irish), ~57k (Scotland), Latin. A self-contained rule engine on the BROAD/SLENDER axis ("caol le caol": a consonant is velarized [Cˠ]/dental next to a/o/u, palatalized [Cʲ] next to e/i) + the SG hallmarks. PRE-ASPIRATION: a medial/final fortis ⟨p t c⟩ → [hp ht̪ xk] after a vowel/sonorant (mac→maxk, cat→kʰaht̪), de-aspirates after an obstruent (asta→as̪t̪), word-initial → aspirated [pʰ t̪ʰ kʰ]; the SLENDER c/t pre-aspirate to [ç] (aice→açkʲ). ⟨b d g⟩ → the UNASPIRATED LENIS [p t̪ k] (NOT Irish's voiced [bˠ d̪ˠ ɡ]); ⟨s⟩ broad→[s̪]/slender→[ʃ]; ⟨l n r⟩ broad→[l̪ˠ n̪ˠ rˠ]/slender→[lʲ ɲ ɾʲ]; lenition bh mh→[v], ch→[x]/[ç], dh gh→[ɣ]/[j], th sh→[h], fh→∅, ph→[f]; ⟨ao⟩→[ɯː], ⟨eu⟩→[iaː]; first-syllable stress + unstressed short vowels→[ə]. **wikipron gla_latn_broad (HUMAN, 6000) — 15.1% FOLDED / 67.0% symbol.** THE FOLDED % IS A MULTI-DIALECT ARTIFACT, NOT a quality signal (the Irish situation, MORE extreme): the referee has 4+ transcriptions per word (Ailean → a-l-a-n / a-l-a-ɲ / ɛ-l-a-ɲ / ɛ-l-ɛ-ɲ) so RAW EXACT is 0.3% (19/6000) and a single output matches only one variant. **Symbol accuracy 67.0% is the honest (modest) signal** (native-only subset 67.0% → NOT name-dragged; the genuine multi-dialect ceiling). The reduction + pre-aspiration + broad/slender are all net-POSITIVE (14.2 vs 9.8 folded with reduction OFF) and spot-checked (mac→maxk EXACT). FOLDS: velarization ˠ (referee marks it variably; broad/slender survives via dental/ʲ/segment), the lenis devoicing-ring (b̥→p, d̪̊→t̪, ɡ̊→k — we never emit a voiced stop), nasalization tilde, and the multi-dialect VOWEL-quality noise (i/ɪ, u/ʊ, ə/ɐ/ɤ, a/ɑ/æ, e/ɛ, o/ɔ). single-source family, REFEREE-LIMITED. Floor 0.12 (below the 15.1%; the folded number is dominated by dialect noise). Deferred: a pronunciation lexicon (the Irish Connacht-lexicon path — the semi-lexical ⟨ea ui ao⟩ + a~ə reduction detail), numbers, a narrow-referee pass.
