        hy: 0.81, // Armenian / հայերեն (hy) — Indo-European (own branch), OWN ALPHABET, EASTERN Armenian (Yerevan). Left-to-right greedy g2p, now via the shared makeArmenianEngine (refactored to also serve Western hyw). wikipron hye_armn_e_broad (HUMAN, 18090): 82.5% FOLDED (up from 81.1% — the shared engine added a no-vowel citation schwa ⟨Բ⟩→[bə] and a C+glide onset exception ⟨Cյ⟩→[Cj] with no schwa, +1.4pp). Signatures: the THREE-WAY stop/affricate system (բ պ փ=b/p/pʰ; ձ ծ ց=d͡z/t͡s/t͡sʰ; ջ ճ չ=d͡ʒ/t͡ʃ/t͡ʃʰ), the UVULARS խ→χ/ղ→ʁ, tap ր→ɾ vs trill ռ→r, the ⟨ու⟩=u digraph, and WORD-INITIAL glides ե→je/ո→vo/և→jev (bare e/o/ev elsewhere). Plus Eastern Armenian SCHWA EPENTHESIS (Vaux) breaking word-initial (գն→gən, խնդ→χənd; s+stop kept: սպ→sp, սկս→skəs) and word-final rising-sonority (եզր zɾ→zəɾ) clusters. NO folds. The 80.6% is REFEREE-BOUNDED: the corpus is very PROPER-NOUN/foreign-name heavy, and (a) foreign names keep their source clusters (Ադրիանա→ɑdɾjɑn, not native-epenthesised) so MEDIAL epenthesis is net-negative and left un-applied, (b) names carry irregular voicing/aspiration (Աբխազիա→ɑpʰχ…). Real-word ~81% ≈ overall (single-letter/acronym noise is only ~1%). Western Armenian (different stop voicing) is a separate dialect, NOT a 2nd referee → single-source. Slavic-style numbers.
        hyw: 0.83, // Western Armenian / արեւմտահայերէն (hyw) — Indo-European (own Armenian branch), Armenian alphabet, the ISTANBUL/DIASPORA standard; SIBLING of Eastern hy, REUSING the shared manifest-driven engine (armenian.ts makeArmenianEngine — hy/hyw differ only in the consonant table + digraphs). wikipron hye_armn_w_broad (HUMAN, 17211): 86.8% FOLDED / 97.8% symbol (BEATS Eastern's 82.5% on the same referee style). THE SIGNATURE = the WESTERN CONSONANT SHIFT — the classical three-way stop/affricate system collapses to a TWO-way one: classical VOICED ⟨բ դ գ ձ ջ⟩ AND classical ASPIRATE ⟨փ թ ք ց չ⟩ both → voiceless-aspirated [pʰ tʰ kʰ t͡sʰ t͡ʃʰ] (they MERGE), while classical VOICELESS ⟨պ տ կ ծ ճ⟩ → VOICED [b d ɡ d͡z d͡ʒ] (պատ→bɑd, բարի→pʰɑɾi, փակ→pʰɑɡ, գործ→kʰoɾd͡z, կով→ɡov). Plus RHOTIC NEUTRALISATION ⟨ր ռ⟩→[ɾ] (Eastern keeps ɾ vs trill r) and the front-rounded ⟨յու/իւ⟩→[ʏ], ⟨յո⟩→[œ] digraphs (loan-heavy). SECONDARY (not floored, 73.7%) = wikipron hye_armn_w_narrow (17584), which MARKS the aspiration our output emits (բարի→pʰɑɾí) — it corroborates the shift; its lower % is transcription-DEPTH detail broad omits (per-word stress, -իա→[jɑ] glides, s-cluster voicelessness). The 1 fold: ASPIRATION ʰ (the BROAD primary doesn't transcribe it — բարի→pɑɾi; the narrow does; the voiced/voiceless-aspirated TWO-way contrast survives the fold). Residual = the same PROPER-NOUN-heavy corpus effects as hy (medial epenthesis left un-applied for foreign clusters, rare voicing-assimilation ʒ→ʃ before a voiceless stop). single-source-FAMILY (broad + narrow both wikipron/Wiktionary, correlated; no epitran hye). Floor 0.83 (below the 86.8% measured). Deferred: numbers verification, the -իա glide (broad omits it), medial epenthesis.
