        kaa: 0.90, // Karakalpak / qaraqalpaq tili (kaa) — KIPCHAK Turkic (close to Kazakh), ~600k (Karakalpakstan, NW Uzbekistan), the 2016 LATIN alphabet (highly phonemic). A greedy digraph+letter scan. THE ORTHOGRAPHY WRITES the uvular/velar choice (no harmony inference, unlike Kazakh): uvular ⟨q⟩→[q] / ⟨x⟩→[χ] / ⟨ǵ⟩→[ʁ] vs velar ⟨k g⟩ / ⟨h⟩; the acute FRONT vowels ⟨á ó ú⟩→[æ ø y] vs back ⟨a o u⟩→[ɑ o u]; the DOTLESS ⟨ı⟩→[ɯ] vs dotted ⟨i⟩→[i]; ⟨ń⟩→[ŋ], ⟨j⟩→[ʒ], ⟨w⟩→[w], ⟨y⟩→[j], digraphs ⟨sh⟩→[ʃ] ⟨ch⟩→[t͡ʃ]; word-final stress. Turkish-I casing handled (dotless capital ⟨I⟩→[ɯ] must lowercase to ⟨ı⟩, not JS's dotted ⟨i⟩ — Ishan→ɯˈʃɑn). **100% FOLDED / 100% symbol** BUT on a TINY 12-word referee (English Wiktionary "Karakalpak terms with IPA pronunciation" — the ONLY source; no wikipron/kaikki/epitran kaa), so the % confirms the vowel + uvular mappings rather than proving broad accuracy. Verified on goldens (qaraqalpaq→qɑrɑqɑlˈpɑq, ǵárezsizlik→ʁærezsizˈlik, xalıq→χɑˈlɯq). THIN single-source. Fold: the referee's syllable dots. Floor 0.90 (below 100%, but the referee is tiny). Deferred: numbers, an independent/larger referee, the Cyrillic front-end.
